{
  "outcome": "resolved",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, good thinking to change it before it expires. Your account is in good shape, and because you're set up with Duo on your phone, you can do this yourself:\n\n1. Go to the Brightline sign-in page and choose the forgot/reset password option. You can also use the change-password option if you're already signed in.\n2. When asked, approve the Duo push on your phone.\n3. Pick a new password that's at least 14 characters long and that you haven't used recently.\n4. On your laptop, lock the screen and sign back in with the new password. It's best to do this while you're on the office network or VPN so the laptop picks up the change. After that, update the password on any other devices that use your account, like your phone's email app.\n\nOne more thing: your mailbox is almost full (about 99%). Once it's full, new email may stop arriving, so it would help to delete or archive old messages, especially ones with large attachments. Just reply if you need help with either of these.",
  "internal_note": "Sender was verified from their own email address. Account: user_id 9, active, 0 failed sign-ins, must_change_password false, not blocked, not VIP. Duo push is enrolled (Duo Mobile on her phone), so per KB-002 she can use self-service reset and I walked her through it. No reset_password needed and no actions queued. Also noticed her mailbox is at 99.4% of quota (50890/51200 MB) and told her to clean it up. Watch for a follow-up ticket about the mailbox.",
